From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 23:14:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07266/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5725: ThinkingCap-27B
 chat-template retest (corrects harness-broken 5724)

REQ-ARC-WMTE-5724 was INCONCLUSIVE for a harness reason: the exp5714 no-fence
induce hits llama.cpp's raw /completion endpoint with no chat template, which
Qwen3.6-family models (ThinkingCap-27B) need for turn structure -> 10/12 reason
cells emitted immediate EOS with ~0 output. This corrects that.

Fix (arc_executable_world_model.py): opt-in LocalGGUFProposer.use_chat_template
routes generate()/complete_text() through /v1/chat/completions so llama-server
applies the GGUF's OWN embedded Qwen3.6 template. Response normalized back to
llama.cpp's {content, stop_type, truncated} shape (finish_reason 'length'->'limit';
split-out reasoning_content folded into content as <think>) so diagnostics/
reason_engaged/overran keep working. Defaults False -> frozen live Qwen3.5-9B raw
path byte-identical. Ruff clean; 19/19 existing proposer tests pass.

exp5725 reuses exp5724.run_reason_cell VERBATIM (only change = use_chat_template
=True); Qwen baseline (1/12) + frozen control (12/12) cited from 5724, not
re-measured (rows tagged reused_from_5724).

Result (adversarial-verify clean): smoke 4/4 <think>-engaged before the run. Full
run - reason_engaged 12/12 (vs 5724's 2/12; degeneracy FIXED, was a harness
artifact not a model limit), completes 3/12 vs Qwen 1/12 (paired +0.167, 3W/2T/1L,
sign-test p=0.625 NOT significant), overran 9/12 vs Qwen 12/12, 0 level-ups,
1/12 plan_found (fragile). Modest direction-only completion gain, not a solved
budget wall. Does NOT flip the frozen live default (operator-only).

